-This method computes a distance field for an isosurface approximation by finding the closest point of the isosurface for every voxel in the volume using a Bounding Volume Hierarchy (BVH) tree. It differs from existing approaches by initializing the upper bound before traversal using sampled points, rather than waiting for the first leaf encounter, which allows for more aggressive pruning at the beginning of the traversal.
